<title>SPAIN: BCH,F.Telecom, D.Telecom, Sprint in Retevision bid.</title>
<headline>BCH,F.Telecom, D.Telecom, Sprint in Retevision bid.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium formed by Banco Central Hispano, France Telecom, Deutsche Telekom and U.S. Sprint said on Monday it would present a bid to buy a 60 percent stake in Retevision.</p>
<p>&quot;Spain's BCH and France Telecom, Deutsche Telekom and Sprint will bid today in the privatisation auction,&quot; a spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Apart from the BCH consortium, Italian state-controlled telecoms group STET said earlier on Monday it had agreed a co-operation telecoms deal with Spanish electricity group Endesa and Union Fenosa.</p>
<p>Today is the first deadline for potential bidders to show interest in the 60 percent offer of Retevision, Spain's second basic telephone operator.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
